{"slug":"bill-keating","qid":"Q775412","name":"Bill Keating","desc":"American politician (born 1952)","article":"Bill Keating","born":"1952-09-06","died":null,"birthplace":"Norwood","parties":["Democratic Party"],"offices":[{"t":"U.S. Representative","w":"MA-09","f":2013,"u":null},{"t":"U.S. Representative","w":"MA-10","f":2011,"u":2013},{"t":"Massachusetts Senate","w":"","f":1985,"u":1999},{"t":"Massachusetts House of Representatives","w":"","f":1977,"u":1985}],"summary":"William Richard Keating (born September 6, 1952) is an American lawyer and politician serving as the U.S. representative for Massachusetts's 9th congressional district since 2013. A member of the Democratic Party, he first entered Congress in 2011, representing Massachusetts's 10th congressional district until redistricting. Keating's district includes Cape Cod and most of the South Coast.","photo":{"f":"bill-keating.jpg","by":"U.S. House of Representatives — Office of the Clerk","lic":"Public domain","licUrl":null,"page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bill_Keating_portrait_(118th_Congress).jpg"},"history":[{"y":2026,"o":"H","k":"MA-09","p":"D","n":"Bill Keating","race":"MA-09"},{"y":2024,"o":"H","k":"MA-09","p":"D","v":251931,"s":56.44,"w":true,"n":"William R. Keating"},{"y":2022,"o":"H","k":"MA-09","p":"D","v":197823,"s":59.17,"w":true,"n":"William R Keating"},{"y":2020,"o":"H","k":"MA-09","p":"D","v":260262,"s":61.3,"w":true,"n":"William R Keating"},{"y":2018,"o":"H","k":"MA-09","p":"D","v":192347,"s":59.38,"w":true,"n":"Bill Keating"},{"y":2016,"o":"H","k":"MA-09","p":"D","v":211790,"s":55.75,"w":true,"n":"William R Keating"},{"y":2014,"o":"H","k":"MA-09","p":"D","v":140413,"s":54.95,"w":true,"n":"William R Keating"},{"y":2012,"o":"H","k":"MA-09","p":"D","v":212754,"s":58.71,"w":true,"n":"William R Keating"},{"y":2010,"o":"H","k":"MA-10","p":"D","v":132743,"s":46.87,"w":true,"n":"William R Keating"}]}